  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Numbered Catalog",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Numbered Catalog\"**\n\nEvery citable thing - a task, a docs page, a drive file, an automation, an incoming event - is a catalog entry with a code you can paste anywhere. The code anchors the row; the name is always readable beside it, never replaced by it. Surfaces are flat, separated by thin hairline rules instead of boxes, and the screen stays calm so the few solid colors that appear can mean something.\n\nDark is the cover: opaque near-black with warm white ink, never pure black. Light is its negative: neutral paper (not cream) with near-black ink. One precise grotesque (Archivo) does all the work, using tabular figures for codes, dates and counts. Color encodes department or state and is never decoration.\n\nThe built layout diverges from the early contract sketch (236px sidebar): it ships as a 64px rail, a 240px context column and a work area, with an optional docked 360px detail panel.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat surfaces; hairlines (rule, rule-strong) do the work of boxes.",
      "Code-first rows: code in tabular figures, name always beside it.",
      "Department color is the one structural color, shown as an inset 3px strip on task rows only.",
      "Signals that are not department or status are ink: solid dot for \"waiting on you\" and \"unread\".",
      "One page-title system: 28px h1 on every destination.",
      "Motion 150-250ms, exponential ease-out, none under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Color-Means-Something Rule",
        "body": "A solid color appears only as department (strip, legend swatch) or status. If a color is neither, it should be ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hue-Neutral Claude Rule",
        "body": "\"Claude working\" is ink, not a hue: no hue was at least 30 degrees clear of all eight departments and the statuses in both themes. Claude is told apart by shape (a 2px dashed pulsing ring), against the solid dot of \"waiting on you\".",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Focus-Only Blue Rule",
        "body": "--focus is for :focus-visible rings (2px, 2px offset) and nothing else.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Amber-On-The-Logo Rule",
        "body": "Brand amber is the logo's alone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Code-Beside-Name Rule",
        "body": "A code is never alone: the name is always readable next to it. In column headers the code is at display scale and the name takes up to two lines.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Group-Heading-Only Rule",
        "body": "Spaced, expanded, uppercase text is for short group headings (Overdue, Today, palette groups, menu groups), never for body or buttons.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Codes, dates and counts use tabular figures (num).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline-Not-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Anything that lives in the page (columns, rows, docked panels, the notifications panel) is separated by a hairline. A shadow is permitted only for a surface that floats over the page momentarily, and it is soft and offset downward, never hard.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use ink, not hue, for any signal that is not a department or a status (waiting, unread, Claude working).",
      "Do put the code in tabular figures beside the name on every row, tile and notification.",
      "Do use the 3px inset strip plus a legend and a \"Department: X\" tooltip for department; carry the name in text too.",
      "Do separate in-page regions with `rule` hairlines (`rule-strong` for floating edges).",
      "Do keep transitions at 150-250ms with `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`, and zero them under `prefers-reduced-motion`.",
      "Do keep the 28px h1 as the single page title on every destination."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use `--focus` blue for anything but focus rings.",
      "Don't put brand amber anywhere except the \"S_\" logo.",
      "Don't show a department strip on projects, tiles or non-task rows.",
      "Don't use monospace (except the logo) or uppercase spaced text outside group headings.",
      "Don't box content in shadowed cards or add decorative gradients.",
      "Don't introduce a new hue for Claude or for state without checking a 30 degree gap from the eight departments."
    ]
  }
}